{%- comment -%}
  snippets/jc-initial-price.liquid

  Emits DATA — the price in cents of the variant the shopper will actually be
  looking at on first paint. No HTML comment banner, for the same reason as the
  other jc-* data snippets.

  WHY THIS IS NOT selected_or_first_available_variant.price
  product__variant-cards-grid.liquid pre-selects the middle value of the first
  option on load (its x-init "popular" pick) whenever that option carries more
  than two values. On Blue that is the 12-can at $35.99, while
  selected_or_first_available_variant is the 4-can at $17.99. Rendering the
  latter server-side puts $17.99 on screen until Alpine's $nextTick corrects it
  — a price flash on load, for a pack that is not the one selected.

  So the server-rendered fallbacks mirror that pre-selection. This is the one
  place the rule is duplicated; the condition below is deliberately the same
  shape as the x-init guard in product__variant-cards-grid.liquid
  (`is_first_option and popular_variant and variant_count > 2`), and when no
  matching variant is found it falls back exactly as that guard does.

  Accepts:
  - product: {object}

  Usage:
    {%- capture jc_initial_price %}{% render 'jc-initial-price', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
    {{ jc_initial_price | plus: 0 | money }}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign initial_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  assign first_option = product.options_with_values.first
  if first_option and first_option.values.size > 2
    assign popular_index = first_option.values.size | minus: 1 | divided_by: 2
    assign popular_value = first_option.values[popular_index] | strip
    for v in product.variants
      if v.options.first == popular_value
        assign initial_variant = v
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
{{- initial_variant.price -}}
